What:		/sys/bus/spmi/devices/<dev>/hib_resume
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	7.4
Contact:	František Balázsy <frantisekbalazsy@gmail.com>
Description:
		(RW) State a resume from hibernation left an Apple SN201202x
		USB Type-C port controller in. Reads one of:

		none
			No resume from hibernation is pending for this port.
		roles-pending
			The controller was restored in place after the cold
			boot behind the resume; the port is revalidated once
			the USB controller that provides its role switch has
			been bound again.
		failed
			The in-place restore failed; the controller has to be
			probed again (unbind and bind the device).

		Writing "roles" while the state is "roles-pending" looks the
		USB role switch up again and revalidates the port, without
		taking the port, or a display on it, down. Other values fail
		with -EINVAL, a write in another state with -EALREADY, and
		-EAGAIN means the USB role switch is not registered yet.
